Package: tailnet-unlock
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: tailnet-unlock contributors <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/foreverworks/tailnet-unlock
Depends: python3 (>= 3.13), initramfs-tools, dropbear-bin, tpm2-tools, libtss2-tcti-device0t64, zfs-initramfs
Recommends: tailscale (>= 1.86)
Conflicts: dropbear-initramfs
Description: unlock an encrypted ZFS root from anywhere on a tailnet
 Puts a small, locked-down SSH door into the initramfs, answering on the
 machine's own address and, with Tailscale, on a tailnet of its own. The door's
 identity is sealed to the machine's TPM, so a copied disk cannot pretend to be
 the box. The root key stays off the machine.
 .
 This package holds the initramfs-tools hook and boot scripts, the door, the
 ZFS key-loading extension and the tailnet-unlock command. It replaces
 dropbear-initramfs, and a dpkg trigger rebuilds the initramfs images whenever
 the tailscaled they carry changes.
